<title>USA: Patterson to buy West-Tex land rigs.</title>
<headline>Patterson to buy West-Tex land rigs.</headline>
<dateline>SNYDER, Texas 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Patterson Energy Inc said on Wednesday it would buy 21 land drilling rigs plus hauling equipment and a yard from West-Tex Drilling Company for $25 million cash plus 283,000 Patterson shares and 200,000 warrants exercisable at $32.00 per Patterson share.</p>
<p>The company said it expects the deal to be completed in the next seven to 10 days.</p>
<p>Patterson has also arranged a $30 million credit agreement with Norwest Bank Texas, of which $15 million will be used to finance the purchase.</p>
<p>Patterson has 66 land-based drilling rigs (60 of which are currently operable) and focuses its operations primarily in Texas and southeast New Mexico.</p>
<p>Its stock closed up 1-1/8 at 40-3/8.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
